OL,3,APoet says being dropped from Senedd
OL,4,Aroyal visit over poem is 'concerning'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWales' national poet has said it is
OL,7,F"quite concerning" that a poem raising
OL,8,Fpolitical issues was rejected from the
OL,9,FSenedd's opening ceremony.
OL,11,FBriefings to the media about the event
OL,12,Fsaid a poetry reading would be made by
OL,13,FHanan Issa at the ceremony on Thursday,
OL,14,Fwhich will be attended by King Charles
OL,15,FIII and Queen Camilla.
OL,17,FBut on Wednesday, Issa posted on social
OL,18,Fmedia that the poem she submitted, To
OL,19,FGrow, which referred to Gaza and trans
OL,20,Fhealthcare, was rejected on the grounds
OL,21,Fthat the ceremony was "apolitical".
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
